# blade-marker.xrs - VR-173 prerequisite 2: is the MEASURED blade where the DRAWN blade is?
#
# The mod measures the held sword's blade from its own drawn mesh (`blade on`) and can show
# the result as two dots (`blade marker on`): the larger at the tip, the smaller at the
# base by the palm. This takes the captures tools\blade-marker-check.py reads, at three
# poses: the blade across the view, the blade low with the head pitched down, and a head
# that is turned, pitched AND ROLLED (a transport that ignores roll agrees with everything
# at a level head).
#
# Needs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY on the dev PC's sewer save, [Mode] GamepadOnly=0.
# Run:   .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\blade-marker.xrs -Dir <sim dir>
# Read:  python tools\blade-marker-check.py <sim dir>\capture poseA
#        python tools\blade-marker-check.py <sim dir>\capture poseA --marker poseA_offset --expect-fail
#        (and the same for poseB and poseC)
#
# Per pose, four captures: the sword drawn with no marker, the marker on, the marker moved
# 10 cm across the blade ON PURPOSE, and (after all three poses) the sword sheathed. The
# offset capture has to FAIL the check, or the check cannot see a marker that is off the
# blade and the passes mean nothing.
#
# The hand is PLACED here (`grip pos`, `grip rot`), which the motion sword reads as a
# tracking jump and discards. `swing off` is sent anyway, so a pose change can never
# become an attack in the middle of a capture. Neither `swing off`, `crosshair dot off`
# nor the `blade` words are written to the ini.
#
# Guards walk under this ledge. A guard behind the blade fattens its silhouette, and the
# check follows the blade as one narrow run to stay on it; a pose whose blade crosses
# something that moves is still the worst case, so look at the <pose>_marker_check_*.png
# overlays (green = measured, red = where the drawn blade ends) before believing a FAIL.

hand r grip pos 0.25 1.30 -0.40; hand r grip rot 0 0 0; head rot 0 0 0
@wait 1500
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500
@mod swing off; crosshair dot off; blade marker off; blade marker offset 0; blade on
@log blade: (LATCHED|measure=1 .* LATCHED) 20s

# A. The blade across the view, head level.
head rot 0 0 0; hand r grip pos -0.35 1.45 -0.80; hand r grip rot 90 0 0
@wait 2500
@shot poseA_drawn
@mod blade marker on
@log blade/marker: drawn 5s
@shot poseA_marker
@mod blade marker offset 0.10
@shot poseA_offset
@mod blade marker offset 0; blade marker off

# B. The blade low, the head pitched 20 degrees down.
head rot 0 -20 0; hand r grip pos -0.25 1.20 -0.75; hand r grip rot 70 25 0
@wait 2500
@shot poseB_drawn
@mod blade marker on
@log blade/marker: drawn 5s
@shot poseB_marker
@mod blade marker offset 0.10
@shot poseB_offset
@mod blade marker offset 0; blade marker off

# C. The head turned 25, pitched 10 up and ROLLED 12; the hand rolled too.
head rot 25 10 12; hand r grip pos -0.45 1.60 -0.70; hand r grip rot 110 -20 30
@wait 2500
@shot poseC_drawn
@mod blade marker on
@log blade/marker: drawn 5s
@shot poseC_marker
@mod blade marker offset 0.10
@shot poseC_offset
@mod blade marker offset 0; blade marker off

# The same three poses with the sword SHEATHED (hold Use): what the view looks like
# without it, which is what makes the silhouette.
btn x press 1500
@wait 4000
head rot 0 0 0; hand r grip pos -0.35 1.45 -0.80; hand r grip rot 90 0 0
@wait 2500
@shot poseA_bare
head rot 0 -20 0; hand r grip pos -0.25 1.20 -0.75; hand r grip rot 70 25 0
@wait 2500
@shot poseB_bare
head rot 25 10 12; hand r grip pos -0.45 1.60 -0.70; hand r grip rot 110 -20 30
@wait 2500
@shot poseC_bare

# Leave it as it was found: the sword drawn, the hand where the other sequences start,
# the measurement and its marker off, the motion sword and the aim dot back on.
head rot 0 0 0; hand r grip pos 0.25 1.30 -0.40; hand r grip rot 0 0 0
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500
@mod blade marker off; blade off; swing on; crosshair dot on
